.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-OBS-CHECK 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-obs-check
.Nd check the metrics and logs stack end to end, and say where it breaks
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -fix
.Op Fl -vm Ar name
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
kldload's observability is a chain: exporters for ZFS, disks and eBPF;
Prometheus scraping them; promtail shipping the journal to Loki; Grafana
drawing both.
A broken link shows up only as an empty dashboard.
.Nm
walks the chain in order, so the first failure is where it breaks:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
the services are active;
.It
each listens on its port;
.It
Prometheus finds every target up;
.It
the ZFS exporter reports pool health, not only its own version;
.It
the SMART exporter sees at least one device;
.It
Loki is ready and has labels;
.It
promtail has shipped something;
.It
the system journal records to disk, asked of
.Xr kldload-journal-assert 8 ;
.It
Grafana answers and has its Loki data source;
.It
each of kldload's dashboards is loaded;
.It
with
.Fl -vm ,
that virtual machine's logs reach the host's Loki.
.El
.Pp
Each failure is followed by the command that shows it.
It changes nothing unless
.Fl -fix
is given.
It must run as root.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -fix
Restart a service that is not active, and run
.Xr kldload-journal-assert 8 ,
which repairs a journal that is not on disk, instead of only asking it.
.It Fl -vm Ar name
Also look for an hour of log lines from
.Ar name
in Loki.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the description at the top of the script and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KLDLOAD_GRAFANA_URL
Where Grafana listens; default
.Lk http://127.0.0.1:3000 ,
since it answers only on loopback, behind the proxy.
.It Ev KLDLOAD_JOURNAL_ASSERT
Another copy of
.Xr kldload-journal-assert 8 ;
for testing.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Every check passed.
.It 1
At least one failed.
.It 2
An unknown argument.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-obs-check
[1] systemd services
  [OK]   zfs_exporter active
  [OK]   smartctl_exporter active
  [OK]   loki active
  [OK]   promtail active
  [OK]   grafana-server active
  [OK]   prometheus active
  [OK]   ebpf_exporter active
\&...
[8] persistent journal
  [OK]   journal: recording persistently in /var/log/journal (root:systemd-journal)

[9] Grafana
  [OK]   Grafana database=ok
  [OK]   Loki datasource provisioned

[10] Grafana dashboards
  [OK]   dashboard zfs-pool-health → 200
\&...
  [OK]   dashboard klab-test-matrix → 200

✓ ALL CHECKS PASSED — observability stack healthy

Dashboards:
  https://10.100.10.121:8443/grafana/d/zfs-pool-health/
\&...
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Pp
Before this page was written, the same machine failed [9] and [10], and
[8] could not have failed:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[9] Grafana
  [FAIL] Grafana /api/health returned ''
  [OK]   Loki datasource provisioned

[10] Grafana dashboards
  [FAIL] dashboard zfs-pool-health → http=000
           ls /var/lib/grafana/dashboards/zfs-pool-health.json
\&...
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload-doctor 8 ,
.Xr kldload-journal-assert 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: the Grafana checks asked for HTTPS on
port 3000, where Grafana speaks plain HTTP on loopback only, so they
failed on every install, and the dashboard links it printed led nowhere;
and its journal check passed whenever an old journal file existed, which
it did on a desktop that had kept its journal only in
.Pa /run
for three weeks.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
.Fl -vm
looks for a Loki label
.Ql vm ;
the desktop above has no such label, and the check has not been seen to
pass.
.Pp
The list of dashboards is fixed in the script.
